{
  "courseSlug": "understanding-tax-implications-of-salary-structuring",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "title": "Chapter 1: Decoding Your CTC",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "CTC vs Gross vs In-Hand: Why Your Offer Letter Number Is Not Your Salary",
          "slug": "ctc-vs-gross-vs-in-hand-why-your-offer-letter-number-is-not-your-salary",
          "body": [
            {
              "_key": "k1",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Riya, a software engineer in Bengaluru, accepts an offer of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k3",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹18 lakh a year",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k4",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ". She divides by 12 and starts planning her life around ₹1,50,000 a month: rent in HSR Layout, a ₹25,000 SIP on Zerodha Coin, a car loan. Her first payslip lands. The number credited to her account is ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k5",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹1,01,917",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k6",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k7",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k8",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Nobody cheated her. She just read the wrong number. This lesson teaches you to read an offer letter the way HR and the tax department read it, so this never happens to you.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "CTC is what you cost your employer. In-hand is what you actually receive. Every salary structuring decision lives in the gap between the two.",
              "_key": "k9"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k10",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k11",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The three numbers hiding in every offer",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k12",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k13",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Every salary in India can be described at three levels. Learn to separate them and every payslip, Form 16 and offer negotiation becomes readable.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k14",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k16",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Cost to Company (CTC)",
                  "marks": [
                    "k15"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k17",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ": everything the company spends on you in a year, whether or not it ever reaches your bank account.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k15",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The total annual amount an employer spends on you, including cash salary, variable pay, its own PF contribution, gratuity provision and insurance premiums."
                }
              ],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k18",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k20",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Gross salary",
                  "marks": [
                    "k19"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k21",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ": the part of CTC that is actually paid to you as salary, before deductions.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k19",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The salary actually payable to you before any deductions: basic, DA, HRA, allowances and bonus. It excludes the employer PF contribution, gratuity provision and group insurance premiums."
                }
              ],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k22",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k24",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "In-hand salary",
                  "marks": [
                    "k23"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k25",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ": what is left after your employee PF, professional tax and income tax are deducted.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k23",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The amount credited to your bank account each month after employee PF, professional tax and TDS are deducted from gross pay. Also called take-home or net pay."
                }
              ],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_type": "comparison",
              "title": "How your employer sees it vs how you experience it",
              "columns": [
                {
                  "_key": "k27",
                  "label": "CTC view (employer)",
                  "points": [
                    "Includes employer PF at 12% of basic",
                    "Includes gratuity set aside for you",
                    "Includes group health insurance premium",
                    "Includes target variable pay, even if not paid in full",
                    "Quoted as a yearly figure, e.g. \"18 LPA\""
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k29",
                  "label": "In-hand view (you)",
                  "points": [
                    "Your own 12% PF is deducted",
                    "Professional tax of up to ₹2,500 a year is deducted",
                    "TDS on salary is deducted every month",
                    "Variable pay arrives only when and if it is paid",
                    "Experienced as a monthly bank credit"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k30"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k31",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k32",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Riya's ₹18 lakh CTC, taken apart",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k33",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k34",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Here is how Riya's employer has structured her ₹18,00,000 CTC for tax year 2026-27. This is a very typical structure for an Indian IT or services company.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "Riya's salary structure (annual CTC ₹18,00,000)",
              "headers": [
                "Component",
                "Annual (₹)",
                "Monthly (₹)",
                "Reaches your account?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k36",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Basic salary (50% of CTC)",
                    "9,00,000",
                    "75,000",
                    "Yes, monthly"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k38",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "House Rent Allowance (40% of basic)",
                    "3,60,000",
                    "30,000",
                    "Yes, monthly"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k40",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Special allowance (balancing figure)",
                    "1,91,400",
                    "15,950",
                    "Yes, monthly"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k42",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Variable pay (target, 10% of CTC)",
                    "1,80,000",
                    "Not monthly",
                    "Yes, once a year, if earned"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k44",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Employer PF contribution (12% of basic)",
                    "1,08,000",
                    "9,000",
                    "No, goes to your EPF account"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k46",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Gratuity provision (4.81% of basic)",
                    "43,269",
                    "Not paid",
                    "No, paid only when you leave after qualifying service"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k48",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Group health and term insurance premium",
                    "17,331",
                    "Not paid",
                    "No, paid to the insurer"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k50",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Total CTC",
                    "18,00,000",
                    "",
                    ""
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k51"
            },
            {
              "_type": "donutChart",
              "title": "Where Riya's ₹18 lakh CTC goes",
              "data": [
                {
                  "_key": "k53",
                  "label": "Basic salary",
                  "value": 900000
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k55",
                  "label": "HRA",
                  "value": 360000
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k57",
                  "label": "Special allowance",
                  "value": 191400
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k59",
                  "label": "Variable pay",
                  "value": 180000
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k61",
                  "label": "Employer PF",
                  "value": 108000
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k63",
                  "label": "Gratuity provision",
                  "value": 43269
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k65",
                  "label": "Insurance",
                  "value": 17331
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k66"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "Special allowance is almost always the balancing figure. HR fixes basic, HRA, PF, gratuity and variable pay first, then whatever is left of the CTC is labelled \"special allowance\". That is why it is often an odd number like ₹1,91,400.",
              "_key": "k67"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k68",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k69",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Step 1: From CTC to gross salary",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k70",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k71",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Strip out everything the employer pays on your behalf but not to you. What remains is the salary that is actually payable to you, which the Income-tax Act, 2025 treats as income from salary under Section 16 (Sections 15 to 17 of the 1961 Act).",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\text{Gross Salary} = \\text{CTC} - \\text{Employer PF} - \\text{Gratuity Provision} - \\text{Insurance Premium}",
              "caption": "Variable pay is part of gross salary only in the year it is actually paid.",
              "_key": "k72"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k73",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k74",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "For Riya: ₹18,00,000 minus ₹1,08,000 minus ₹43,269 minus ₹17,331 gives an annual gross salary of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k75",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹16,31,400",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k76",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ", including the full variable pay. Her fixed gross, the part paid every month, is ₹14,51,400, or ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k77",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹1,20,950 a month",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k78",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "quiz",
              "title": "Spot the non-salary item",
              "question": "Which of these is part of Riya's CTC but NOT part of her gross salary?",
              "options": [
                "House Rent Allowance",
                "Special allowance",
                "Employer's contribution to PF",
                "Basic salary"
              ],
              "correctIndex": 2,
              "explanation": "The employer's 12% PF contribution is deposited directly into Riya's EPF account. It is a cost to the company and a long-term benefit to her, but it is never paid out as salary, so it sits in CTC but not in gross salary. HRA, special allowance and basic are all paid to her every month.",
              "_key": "k79"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "By law, employer PF is mandatory only on basic pay up to ₹15,000 a month. Many companies, like Riya's, contribute 12% of the full basic anyway. Chapter 1, Lesson 3 covers how this choice changes both your CTC and your in-hand pay.",
              "_key": "k80"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k81",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k82",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Step 2: From gross salary to in-hand",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k83",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k84",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Three deductions come out of gross pay before a single rupee reaches Riya's account:",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k85",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k86",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Employee PF",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k87",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ": 12% of basic, so ₹9,000 a month. This is still her money, sitting in EPF and earning interest, but she cannot spend it today.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k88",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k90",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Professional tax",
                  "marks": [
                    "k89"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k91",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ": ₹200 a month in Karnataka (₹300 in February), capped at ₹2,500 a year.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k89",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "A state-level tax on employment, capped at ₹2,500 a year by the Constitution. Karnataka and Maharashtra deduct ₹200 a month and ₹300 in February."
                }
              ],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k92",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k94",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "TDS on salary",
                  "marks": [
                    "k93"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k95",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ": your employer estimates your tax for the whole year and deducts it in roughly equal monthly slices.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k93",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "Tax Deducted at Source: income tax your employer estimates on your full-year salary and deducts in monthly instalments before paying you."
                }
              ],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\text{In-hand (monthly)} = \\text{Monthly Gross} - \\text{Employee PF} - \\text{Professional Tax} - \\text{TDS}",
              "caption": "Monthly in-hand for fixed pay, before any variable pay or reimbursements.",
              "_key": "k96"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k97",
              "_type": "collapsible",
              "title": "Show the working: how Riya's TDS of about ₹9,833 a month is calculated",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_key": "k98",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k99",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Riya is in the new tax regime, which is the default for tax year 2026-27. Her employer projects her full-year salary like this:",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k100",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k101",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Gross salary including target variable pay: ₹16,31,400",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "number",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k102",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k103",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Less standard deduction under Section 19 of the Income-tax Act, 2025 (Section 16 of the 1961 Act): ₹75,000",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "number",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k104",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k105",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Taxable salary: ₹15,56,400",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "number",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k106",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k107",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Tax on slabs: 0 on the first ₹4,00,000, ₹20,000 on ₹4 to 8 lakh, ₹40,000 on ₹8 to 12 lakh, and ₹53,460 on the remaining ₹3,56,400 at 15%. Total ₹1,13,460",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "number",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k108",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k109",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "No rebate under Section 156 (Section 87A of the 1961 Act), because taxable income is above ₹12,00,000",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "number",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k110",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k111",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Add 4% health and education cess: ₹1,17,998, rounded to ₹1,18,000",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "number",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k112",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k113",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Spread over 12 months: about ₹9,833 a month",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "number",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_type": "table",
                  "caption": "New regime slabs, tax year 2026-27",
                  "headers": [
                    "Taxable income slab",
                    "Rate"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k115",
                      "_type": "tableRow",
                      "cells": [
                        "Up to ₹4,00,000",
                        "Nil"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k117",
                      "_type": "tableRow",
                      "cells": [
                        "₹4,00,001 to ₹8,00,000",
                        "5%"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k119",
                      "_type": "tableRow",
                      "cells": [
                        "₹8,00,001 to ₹12,00,000",
                        "10%"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k121",
                      "_type": "tableRow",
                      "cells": [
                        "₹12,00,001 to ₹16,00,000",
                        "15%"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k123",
                      "_type": "tableRow",
                      "cells": [
                        "₹16,00,001 to ₹20,00,000",
                        "20%"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k125",
                      "_type": "tableRow",
                      "cells": [
                        "₹20,00,001 to ₹24,00,000",
                        "25%"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "_key": "k127",
                      "_type": "tableRow",
                      "cells": [
                        "Above ₹24,00,000",
                        "30%"
                      ]
                    }
                  ],
                  "_key": "k128"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k129",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k130",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "In practice employers recalculate TDS during the year as actual variable pay, declarations and proofs come in, so the monthly figure moves a little. Chapter 5 covers declarations and proofs.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "k131",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k132",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "So Riya's monthly in-hand works out as ₹1,20,950 minus ₹9,000 minus ₹200 minus ₹9,833, which is ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k133",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹1,01,917",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k134",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "k136",
                  "label": "CTC per month",
                  "value": "₹1,50,000",
                  "context": "₹18 lakh divided by 12"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k138",
                  "label": "Fixed gross per month",
                  "value": "₹1,20,950",
                  "context": "Basic + HRA + special allowance"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k140",
                  "label": "In-hand per month",
                  "value": "₹1,01,917",
                  "context": "After PF, professional tax and TDS"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k142",
                  "label": "Monthly gap",
                  "value": "₹48,083",
                  "context": "About 32% of CTC per month"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k143"
            },
            {
              "_type": "chart",
              "chartType": "bar",
              "title": "Riya's year: from CTC to money in the bank",
              "xAxisLabel": "Stage",
              "yAxisLabel": "₹ per year",
              "data": [
                {
                  "_key": "k145",
                  "label": "CTC",
                  "value": 1800000
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k147",
                  "label": "Gross salary",
                  "value": 1631400
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k149",
                  "label": "Taxable salary",
                  "value": 1556400
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k151",
                  "label": "Take-home (incl. variable)",
                  "value": 1402900
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k152"
